        },
        "committer": {
          "name": "Artem Blagodarenko",
          "email": "ablagodarenko@thelustrecollective.com",
          "date": "2026-10-14 20:05:02.000000000",
          "tz": 60
        },
        "subject": "LU-20966 tests: make sanity 17h inject a live create failure",
        "message": "LU-20966 tests: make sanity 17h inject a live create failure\n\nsanity test_17h is meant to check that the MDS does not LBUG while\nfreeing the layout after a failed striped create. It armed\nOBD_FAIL_MDS_LOV_PREP_CREATE (0x141), but that value is only a #define\nin lustre/include/obd_support.h and no CFS_FAIL_CHECK site uses it.\nThe test also discarded touch's exit status with \"|| true\". As a\nresult it only did an ordinary create, never ran any stripe-\npreparation error unwind, and could not fail.\n\nThe test now arms OBD_FAIL_MDS_ALLOC_OBDO (0x128) on the MDS that\nserves the directory. That fail point is still checked at the top of\nlod_declare_striped_create() in lustre/lod/lod_object.c, where it\nreturns -ENOMEM and frees the layout already initialised from the\ndirectory default through lod_striping_free(). The test now requires\nthe create to fail. It then clears fail_loc and requires a second\nfully striped create to succeed, which shows the MDS survived the\nunwind. The directory is created with \"-c 1\" so that \"lfs getdirstripe\n-i\" names the MDT that actually handles the create, and the setup\ncommands now check their return codes.\n\nWith the patch applied, the fail point fired once on the serving MDS.\nThe -ENOMEM from lod_declare_striped_create() reached the client\nthrough mdd_create() and mdt_reint_open(), and the following 8-stripe\ncreate succeeded. Note that this fail point fires before any stripe\nobject is reserved, so the cleanup it exercises is shallow.\n\nFound-by: dyntest\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial testlist=sanity env=ONLY=17h,ONLY_REPEAT=10 mdscount=2 mdtcount=4\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5-5\nSigned-off-by: Artem Blagodarenko <ablagodarenko@thelustrecollective.com>\nChange-Id: I9ef8a831b68f1a2ee2a0cb3d2172a8cf9bbee144\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
  },
